1
00:03:52,173 --> 00:03:58,173
It feeds on the darkness within.

2
00:07:44,347 --> 00:07:50,347
The Assent is a horror, thriller film directed by Pearry Reginald Teo.

3
00:11:36,521 --> 00:11:42,521
After a series of disturbing supernatural events in his home, Joel a young
single father, comes to suspect that his young son may be possessed.

4
00:15:28,695 --> 00:15:34,695
Soon Joel receives a visit from Father Lambert, a controversial exorcist
in town whose last patient died during his treatment.

5
00:19:20,869 --> 00:19:26,869
As increasing chilling occurrences begin to unfold, the priest informs a resistant Joel that unless he
can successfully perform an exorcism, the devil will soon take full control of his boy.

6
00:23:13,043 --> 00:23:19,043
Joel, played by Robert Kazinsky.

7
00:27:05,217 --> 00:27:11,217
Father Lambert, played by Peter Jason.

8
00:30:57,391 --> 00:31:03,391
Cassie, played by Hannah Ward.

9
00:34:49,565 --> 00:34:55,565
Dr. Hawkins, played by Tatum O'Neal.

10
00:38:41,739 --> 00:38:47,739
Mason, played by Caden Dragomer.

11
00:42:33,913 --> 00:42:39,913
Brother Michael, played by Douglas Spain.

12
00:46:26,086 --> 00:46:32,086
Royal assent is the method by which a monarch formally approves an act of the
legislature, either directly or through an official acting on the monarch's behalf.

13
00:50:18,260 --> 00:50:24,260
In some jurisdictions, royal assent is equivalent to
promulgation, while in others that is a separate step.

14
00:54:10,434 --> 00:54:16,434
Under a modern constitutional monarchy, royal assent is
considered little more than a formality.

15
00:58:02,608 --> 00:58:08,608
Even in nations such as the United Kingdom, Norway, the Netherlands, Liechtenstein and Monaco which still, in theory, permit their monarch to
withhold assent to laws, the monarch almost never does so, except in a dire political emergency or on advice of government.

16
01:01:54,782 --> 01:02:00,782
While the power to veto by withholding royal assent was once exercised often by European
monarchs, such an occurrence has been very rare since the eighteenth century.

17
01:05:46,956 --> 01:05:52,956
Royal assent is typically associated with elaborate ceremony.

18
01:09:39,130 --> 01:09:45,130
In the United Kingdom the Sovereign may appear personally in the House of Lords or may appoint Lords Commissioners, who
announce that royal assent has been granted at a ceremony held at the Palace of Westminster for this purpose.

19
01:13:31,304 --> 01:13:37,304
Royal assent is usually granted less ceremonially by letters patent.

20
01:17:23,478 --> 01:17:29,478
In other nations, such as Australia, the governor-general (as the Monarch's
representative) has the right to dissolve the parliament and to sign a bill.

21
01:21:15,652 --> 01:21:21,652
In Canada, the governor general may give assent either in person at a ceremony in the Senate or
by a written declaration notifying Parliament of their agreement to the bill.

22
01:25:07,826 --> 01:25:13,826
The tone is dark and intense.
